          "linkId": "dm-ed",
          "text": "Diabetes can damage retinal blood vessels before you notice a change in sight. A dilated exam (and often photos or OCT) is how we catch this. Keep A1c, blood pressure, and cholesterol at the targets your PCP set. Call promptly for sudden blur, a shower of floaters, or a curtain over vision. Yearly exams are the minimum; some patients need to return sooner.",
